#### Example 1: S3 Lifecycle Policy for Healthcare Transaction Data (HTD)

```json
{
  "Rules": [
    {
      "Id": "HTD-6-Year-Retention-Policy",
      "Status": "Enabled",
      "Filter": {
        "And": {
          "Tags": [
            {
              "Key": "DataClassification",
              "Value": "HTD"
            },
            {
              "Key": "ComplianceRequirement",
              "Value": "HIPAA"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "Transitions": [
        {
          "Days": 30,
          "StorageClass": "STANDARD_IA"
        },
        {
          "Days": 90,
          "StorageClass": "GLACIER"
        },
        {
          "Days": 2160,
          "StorageClass": "DEEP_ARCHIVE"
        }
      ],
      "Expiration": {
        "Days": 2190
      },
      "NoncurrentVersionTransitions": [
        {
          "NoncurrentDays": 30,
          "StorageClass": "GLACIER"
        }
      ],
      "NoncurrentVersionExpiration": {
        "NoncurrentDays": 90
      }
    },
    {
      "Id": "OTD-90-Day-Retention-Policy",
      "Status": "Enabled",
      "Filter": {
        "Tag": {
          "Key": "DataClassification",
          "Value": "OTD"
        }
      },
      "Transitions": [
        {
          "Days": 30,
          "StorageClass": "STANDARD_IA"
        }
      ],
      "Expiration": {
        "Days": 90
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

**Explanation**: This S3 lifecycle policy implements two retention strategies based on data classification tags. Healthcare Transaction Data (HTD) tagged with `DataClassification=HTD` and `ComplianceRequirement=HIPAA` follows 6-year retention per HIPAA §164.316: Days 0-30 in S3 Standard ($23/TB-month), Days 31-90 in Standard-IA ($16/TB-month, 30% savings), Days 91-2160 in Glacier ($4/TB-month, 83% savings), Days 2161-2190 in Deep Archive ($1/TB-month, 96% savings), automatic deletion on Day 2191 (6 years + buffer). Operational Telemetry Data (OTD) follows 90-day retention with transition to Standard-IA on Day 30 and deletion on Day 91. Policy includes noncurrent version handling for versioned buckets transitioning old versions to Glacier after 30 days and deleting after 90 days.

**Use Case**: Claims processing system storing claims records, EOBs (Explanation of Benefits), and provider remittance advice requiring HIPAA 6-year retention. System tags claim files with `DataClassification=HTD` and application logs with `DataClassification=OTD`, enabling automated lifecycle management without manual intervention.

